# =============================================================================
# flow/lec_pipe_equiv.ys -- equivalence of the retimed (pipelined) FIR
# =============================================================================
# Obligation, stated precisely:
#
#     fir_top_pipe.dout(t) == fir_top_tree.dout(t - 2)   for all t and all inputs
#
# fir_top_tree and fir_top_pipe instantiate the SAME balanced adder tree; the
# only difference is that fir_top_pipe has two register cuts inside it. So this
# is a pure *retiming* equivalence, and the criterion is deliberately expressed
# as a shifted output sequence: a pipeline does not produce the same value at the
# same cycle, it produces the same sequence two clocks later.
#
# The harness rtl/lec_pipe_wrapper.v delays the reference output by exactly the
# added latency and asserts equality on every cycle from reset, so there is no
# "pipeline fill" window that has to be excused.
#
# SCOPE OF THE RESULT -- read this before quoting it
# --------------------------------------------------
# This script runs a BOUNDED sequential proof: from the all-zero reset state, no
# counterexample exists within the stated depth (-seq). The depth below is set
# from the design itself (LATENCY_SHIFT + 2 = 4), comfortably past the pipeline
# fill, so it covers the transient as well as the steady state.
#
# It is NOT an unbounded proof, and the script does not pretend otherwise:
# `sat -tempinduct` was also attempted, and its outcome is recorded in the
# README. Temporal induction from an *arbitrary* initial state legitimately fails
# here, because "the reference delay line holds the values the pipeline needs" is
# a reachable-state invariant, not a state predicate -- induction would require
# that invariant to be supplied explicitly.
# =============================================================================

read_verilog -formal -I rtl rtl/fir_sum.v rtl/fir_core.v rtl/fir_top.v rtl/lec_pipe_wrapper.v
prep -top lec_pipe_wrapper -flatten

# The FIR resets asynchronously; SAT has no model for async FFs.
async2sync

# --- bounded proof from the reset state --------------------------------------
sat -verify -prove-asserts -seq 4 -set-init-zero -show-ports
